cargo-zempic 0.0.1
    workspace: [WORKSPACE_ROOT]  (1 members, 1 selected)
      profile: release  (inherits: none)
optimizing for: size
       target: x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu

TIER 2  COMPILER                                                      2 findings

  HIGH   none   config/link-dead-code            .cargo/config.toml
        effort: trivial   runtime cost: none   fix: safe
        `build.rustflags` in
        `[WORKSPACE_ROOT]/.cargo/config.toml`
        sets `-C link-dead-code`, which keeps symbols the linker would otherwise
        discard.
        Tradeoff: The flag increases size; rarely intended outside coverage runs. Like any
        rustflags change, removing it invalidates the whole build cache, costing
        a full rebuild.
  MEDIUM moderate config/link-gc-sections          unset -> -C link-arg=-Wl,--gc-sections
        effort: trivial   runtime cost: none   fix: consequential
        `build.rustflags` in
        `[WORKSPACE_ROOT]/.cargo/config.toml`
        sets `-C link-dead-code`, which suppresses rustc's own
        section-garbage-collection default. `config/link-dead-code` reports the
        flag itself; this finding reports the linker consequence and the flag
        that restores the behavior.
        Tradeoff: Platform-specific: `--gc-sections` on ELF, `-dead_strip` on Mach-O. Like
        any rustflags change, adding it invalidates the whole build cache,
        costing a full rebuild.
SUMMARY
  2 findings: 1 high, 1 medium.  By magnitude: 1 moderate, 1 none.
  2 auto-fixable.

  Magnitude is an ordinal judgement, not a measurement. zempic does not build
  and does not read compiled artifacts, so it reports no sizes.
